  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XC">Lemma <span data-tag="00XC">7.15.2</span>.</a> Given a morphism of sites $f : \mathcal{D} \to \mathcal{C}$ corresponding to the functor $u : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ the pair of functors $(f^{-1} = u_ s, f_* = u^ s)$ is a morphism of topoi $\mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{D}) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (\mathcal{C})$. </p>
